          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is marine collagen better than bovine collagen?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not meaningfully for most people. Marine collagen is mostly type I and bovine is mostly types I and III, but both are digested into similar amino acids and peptides. Marine collagen suits pescatarians and people who avoid beef, while bovine is usually cheaper. Anyone with a fish allergy should avoid marine collagen and multi-collagen blends that include fish."
          }
        },
